This product is the Cangjie (仓颉) / HarmonyOS counterpart of the EU Digital
Identity Wallet RQES (Remote Qualified Electronic Signature) layer. Its
signing surface mirrors the iOS PodofoWrapper / Android PoDoFoWrapper of:

    eudi-lib-podofo
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-podofo

The CSC client, RQES kit and RQES UI domain modules (eudi_cjrqes_csc,
eudi_cjrqes_kit, eudi_cjrqes_ui) are Cangjie ports of:

    eudi-lib-ios-rqes-csc-swift, eudi-lib-ios-rqes-kit, eudi-lib-ios-rqes-ui
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet

The Cangjie sources and the C ABI bridge (native/bridge/) are licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0 (below).

The vendored native library libpodofo_rqes.so is a separate work that
statically links the following third-party software, each under its own
licence. The build recipes in native/recipes/ and native/REBUILD.md identify
the exact upstream sources and reproduce the binary:

  - PoDoFo, EUDI fork eudi-lib-podofo 0.3.8 (LGPL-2.0-or-later)
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-podofo
  - OpenSSL 1.1.1u (OpenSSL License and Original SSLeay License)
    https://www.openssl.org/
  - FreeType 2.13.0 (FreeType License (FTL) or GPL-2.0, at your option;
    used here under the FTL)
    https://freetype.org/
  - libxml2 2.11.3 (MIT License)
    https://github.com/GNOME/libxml2
  - libpng 1.6.39 (PNG Reference Library License version 2)
    http://www.libpng.org/pub/png/libpng.html
  - zlib 1.3.1 (zlib License), linked statically and hidden so it cannot
    clash with other zlib copies in the host process
    https://zlib.net/

